{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/102401-aberrant-s-deal","id":102401,"title":"Aberrant's \"deal\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-30T22:26:55-07:00","id":102401,"title":"Aberrant's \"deal\"","content":"What, exactly, is the deal with Aberrant? I've gathered it's a kind of superhero roleplaying game in which the superpowered characters ('novas'?) were activated by some kind of celestial event, but apart from that, I'm a bit vague.<br /> <br /> What's it about? What are the themes? Is it &quot;superheroes trying to fit into society&quot;, or &quot;superheroes being awesome&quot;, a mix, something different? What system does it use, I've found references to a d20 but has that been widely adopted, or is it kind of ignored? Most importantly, is it fun, or kind of annoying without the right ST?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T23:15:16-07:00","id":102427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/102401-aberrant-s-deal#post102401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, exactly, is the deal with Aberrant? I've gathered it's a kind of superhero roleplaying game in which the superpowered characters ('novas'?) were activated by some kind of celestial event, but apart from that, I'm a bit vague.<br /> <br /> What's it about? What are the themes? Is it &quot;superheroes trying to fit into society&quot;, or &quot;superheroes being awesome&quot;, a mix, something different? What system does it use, I've found references to a d20 but has that been widely adopted, or is it kind of ignored? Most importantly, is it fun, or kind of annoying without the right ST?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aberrant falls into the supers sub-genre that explores the impact supers have on the world, akin to the Authority.<br /> <br /> As far as the public is concerned, the explosion of the space station Galatea in 1998 triggered the eruption of superhumans - novas - around the world, people who draw on the quantum forces of the universe to accomplish incredible things. (That's not the _whole_ truth, but it's close enough to be useful.)<br /> <br /> As a nova, you're a celebrity, a superstar, in the making. What are you going to do with that incredible power? What mark will you make on the world?<br /> <br /> There's a catch, though: quantum power comes with the chance of Taint, which represents a nova's mind and body becoming transformed, moving further and further away from humanity. They can be incredibly beautiful, or incredibly monstrous, but they're becoming inhuman. Power has its price.<br /> <br /> Aberrant 1e uses a variant of the cWOD Storyteller system; a d20 version was released after the line was cancelled, but people generally focus on the ST version. 2e - along with the rest of the Continuum - will be using a brand new d10-based system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T23:43:22-07:00","id":102448,"title":"","content":"How does it actually play? Any irritating tendencies, or bits that work really well? I've read a little about Mega-Attributes, do they have the same issues as Epic Attributes from Scion (some being just obscenely useful, while others not so much)? What are your main adversaries: other Novas, monsters, or is it a &quot;shaping the world to suit your will&quot; deal? How does it handle higher level characters: well, or badly (some systems do handle one well but tank the other, after all)? Is there any real way humans can stand against Novas, should a Nova decide, eg that New York is now his fiefdom? Or is that the kind of thing other Novas tend to handle out of self-preservation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T00:49:23-07:00","id":102483,"title":"","content":"It's a dark parody of celebrity culture. Basically, what happens if we just took a bunch of regular schmucks, and gave them godlike power and undeserved fame, fortune, and influence without them doing jack shit to earn it? Turns out they nearly destroy the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does it actually play? Any irritating tendencies, or bits that work really well? I've read a little about Mega-Attributes, do they have the same issues as Epic Attributes from Scion (some being just obscenely useful, while others not so much)? What are your main adversaries: other Novas, monsters, or is it a &quot;shaping the world to suit your will&quot; deal? How does it handle higher level characters: well, or badly (some systems do handle one well but tank the other, after all)? Is there any real way humans can stand against Novas, should a Nova decide, eg that New York is now his fiefdom? Or is that the kind of thing other Novas tend to handle out of self-preservation? </div> </div> </div>Your biggest opponents will likely be other Novas, and some human organizations. The game is extremely high power, and thus it becomes less a matter of how you solve problems and more a matter of what you choose to do with that power. There are a handful of high end games like this, and that's pretty much the way to handle them. Most of the Mega-Attributes are useful. There are some complaints about Mega-Strength, because of the way it scales.It winds up being balanced in a rock-paper-scissors sort of way. I wouldn't call anything not useful though.As for humans versus Nova, a lot depends on the Nova but for the most part, not really. Humanity mostly wins the war because the Novas don't want to squish everyone, so they leave.<br /> <br /> Personally I like it for being a superhero game with one staple origin (which I think works better for these things) and for being the fastest to build a character in of any reasonably complex I've tried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T00:58:31-07:00","id":102486,"title":"","content":"So, from what you've said, it sounds sort of like Exalted, only in a modern setting without all the ex-Primordial issues: you're suddenly a superhero, what will you do with this power?<br /> <br /> That does sound intriguing. I have been looking for a superhero game (it's a major genre that I have yet to play), see if I can find someone to play it with.<br /> <br /> What are some common game types? &quot;This part of the world is unstable due to X, Y and Z factors: go fix it&quot; seems an obvious one. Googling just comes up with a bunch of crochet stuff","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T02:50:53-07:00","id":102517,"title":"","content":"Each of the Allegiances in the game have a different take on what you\u2019re supposed to be doing:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Aberrants: you\u2019re on the run from a shadowy organization that has it in for you. Games featuring these self-styled Aberrants tend to have something of an X-Men vibe to them. <br /> \u2022 Project Utopia: you just joined the Avengers. <br /> \u2022 Project Proteus: you\u2019re the guys who do the dirty work that Project Utopia can\u2019t. <br /> \u2022 The Teregen: you\u2019re a god amongst men; act like it!<br /> \u2022 The Directive: welcome to SHIELD. <br /> <br /> There are also government- and corporate-sponsored Novas and individualists who have no allegiance to anyone but themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T07:56:55-07:00","id":102619,"title":"","content":"It's definitely not a &quot;regular&quot; superhero game, it's a deconstruction of the genre (among other things) - there's no Marvel and DC style setting of &quot;it's like the real world apart from some superheroes and supervillains fighting&quot;, as the setting has already changed dramatically in the ten years between the first novas' appearance and the game's official start date.<br /> <br /> Divorced from the setting, the rules cover most things a superhero game would need, but setting elements like the warping effects of high power are built into the system so it would still take effort to make it &quot;generic&quot;.<br /> <br /> The official adventures (the <b>Aberrant Worldwide</b> series) focus on conspiracies, major public displays of nova power, and nova-on-nova conflict. They're probably the most &quot;superhero&quot; part of the game line, in fact, although they're still pretty high stakes. In one adventure, a nova runs for President - and it includes a sidebar on what to do if one of the player characters wants to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T15:43:41-07:00","id":104383,"title":"","content":"Coolio, very helpful. So the Allegiance the characters belong to will sort-of inform the kind of adventures they'll have, insofar that's the sort of issue they'll get orders to deal with?<br /> <br /> Given that I assume Novas are still freakishly rare (after a flip through a pdf of the book, I remember the figure 6,000?), and most Novas join an allegiance due to the advantages of them, they don't get overly upset about what a Nova does on their 'spare time'? How much control do they try to exert? Or are they more philosophical associations, espousing certain values?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T16:06:24-07:00","id":104405,"title":"","content":"It's a sliding scale. Project Utopia will probably have very strict rules for their nova employees -- they are VERY concerned with PR and public image -- while the Teragen is extraordinarily laissez-faire, and more of a philosophical association.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T17:14:24-07:00","id":105913,"title":"","content":"Managed to get a copy of the core book on the cheap off eBay, so that's cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Based on what I read in the PDF, I get the feeling most people have a bit of a mixed feelings about the Novas? On the one hand, they have objectively done a lot to make the world a nicer place, but on the other hand, people being people wouldn't be entirely comfortable with people being able to explode things with their brains. I mean, people get pretty worried about automatic weapons (no, I'm not weighing in on that, I'm in Australia where we don't think you need <i>any</i> guns, plus Americas laws are Americas business, as baffling as I find them), and while you can't ban people...usually, I can see that fear breeding mistrust, to a point? And that group, Teregen? The one that basically says 'Novas are superior, bow down to us' in the introductory stuff? Doubt they'd help the situation; if nothing else they'd serve as a justification for peoples pre-existing fears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T23:38:38-07:00","id":106073,"title":"","content":"It works out both ways. The Teragen work as a catalyst to justify human fear/distrust of novas, and Project Utopia's secret manipulation and culling of novas works to fuel an us versus them mentality in novas in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T00:52:34-07:00","id":106111,"title":"","content":"There's also an inherent yet subtle... I don't want to say HATRED, maybe jealousy? At first, baselines adore novas -- they're cool, they're hip, they're SHOOTING LASERS OUT OF THEIR EYES THAT'S AWESOME! But once that wears off, people start to become jealous of novas. Think about it this way: you are an artist. Say, a novelist, or playwright. You have spent your entire life perfecting your art, correcting mistakes and building upon your successes. DECADES of work have gone into your passion. Then some jerk with a quantum-powered tumor in his brain gets a headache while reading Shakespeare, and in the span of a Planck moment suddenly becomes a writer ORDERS OF MAGNITUDE greater than you -- WITH NO EFFORT INTO GAINING THE SKILLS. You'd have some bruised ego. To make matters worse, you'd know that no matter how hard you push yourself or practice or work, nothing you do can come close -- anything you can do, he can do better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T01:55:30-07:00","id":106146,"title":"","content":"That makes sense. And ripe for potential story hooks with sympathetic if somewhat unchallenging antagonists! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T22:03:06-07:00","id":120162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/102401-aberrant-s-deal?p=106146#post106146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes sense. And ripe for potential story hooks with sympathetic if somewhat unchallenging antagonists! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on situation - not all novas are built equal and human beings can still be smart, canny and dastardly as always. Novas have advantages but planning and preparation can still do wonders. Not to mention strategic use of nova related medicines and stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T11:57:32-07:00","id":120442,"title":"","content":"I suppose a good example of Human vs Nova -- and how the baseline could still win -- would be the Black Widow vs Loki scene in The Avengers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T18:49:39-07:00","id":120656,"title":"","content":"Black Widow is clearly a Dare Devil, which in the new systems terms probably is a Talent. Baseline vs Nova Loki is Agent Coulson. That cool ass gun he uses is how Baselines could still win against a Nova.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T19:37:27-07:00","id":120672,"title":"","content":"Ah, and then we get into the discussion of just how &quot;not baseline&quot; a Daredevil or Talent is. But, yes, you're right; she's obviously Inspired in some small manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T21:53:19-07:00","id":120739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/102401-aberrant-s-deal?p=120656#post120656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Widow is clearly a Dare Devil, which in the new systems terms probably is a Talent. Baseline vs Nova Loki is Agent Coulson. That cool ass gun he uses is how Baselines could still win against a Nova.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/102401-aberrant-s-deal?p=120672#post120672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, and then we get into the discussion of just how &quot;not baseline&quot; a Daredevil or Talent is. But, yes, you're right; she's obviously Inspired in some small manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what either of you are talking about, so I'm just going to assume that she is what she is in the movies: a highly-trained, skilled human.<br /> <br /> Which is probably easier to understand, and doesn't require me to attempt to synthesise two different systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T22:54:08-07:00","id":120773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/102401-aberrant-s-deal?p=120739#post120739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea what either of you are talking about, so I'm just going to assume that she is what she is in the movies: a highly-trained, skilled human.<br /> <br /> Which is probably easier to understand, and doesn't require me to attempt to synthesise two different systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Daredevils/Talents are people whose thing is being exceptionally lucky or exceptionally skilled, ala Black Widow and Hawkeye. If Novas are superheroes, Talents are action heroes.<br /> <br /> They come from the other Continuum games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T13:58:40-07:00","id":121178,"title":"","content":"To try and tie that all back to your original question, one of the (many) themes of Aberrant is the superiority of Novas compared with regular (baseline) humans. Some Novas are a bit, shall we say, &quot;uppity&quot;, and love to flaunt their superiority or do bad things with a(n) (imagined) guarantee that they are untouchable. One way to play in an Aberrant game is to not play as Novas at all, but instead play normal humans who are trying to keep other people safe from the &quot;bad&quot; Novas. Most of the time, that would be using the mostly-baseline organization, The Directive.<br /> <br /> Essentially, it's SHIELD vs Supervillains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T10:21:54-07:00","id":121824,"title":"","content":"<br /> Just to add a little more variety - there is also the special Ultimate Fighting Leagues (ala WWF) and the Mercenary ranks (Totentanz! Devries Consulting), which focus on either entertainment or the weaponizing of Novas for profit.<br /> <br /> The weakest portion of the game is the Crafting of super tech - it's not bad, but Adventure had a more mature system.<br /> <br /> Also fan books of each Mega Attribute set exists - Physical, Social and Mental.<br /> <br /> A slight warning - the super tech and the &quot;physics&quot; of the powers are not capable to real-science, and not generally mass-producible. So Nova's are of value to maintain and produce the tech and effects. Which can add to the adventure an aspect of gilded cage for some power sets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1336-gideon","name":"Gideon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T17:31:24-07:00","id":122099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gideon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/102401-aberrant-s-deal?p=121824#post121824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A slight warning - the super tech and the &quot;physics&quot; of the powers are not capable to real-science, and not generally mass-producible. So Nova's are of value to maintain and produce the tech and effects. Which can add to the adventure an aspect of gilded cage for some power sets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually prefer that. Makes it more, magical? special? If everyone can blast eye lasers with the right contact lenses, it makes Novas who can do the same thing somewhat less 'special'.<br /> <br /> But that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T00:42:32-07:00","id":128798,"title":"","content":"Thematically Aberrant has more in common with Watchmen than it does the mainline superhero stuff since it deals with questions like &quot;what is the upper limit of human?&quot; and things like that. It also has a cold stream of reality running though it; many things that are handwaved away in the comics are explored in Aberrant, like the effects of fame on both the super and the world around her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}